mittee and the Committee of Regions. 29 November 2002, Brussels.</article-title><comment>Available: <ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://europa.eu.int/eur-lex/lex/LexUriServ/site/en/com/2002/com2002_0667en01.pdf">http://europa.eu.int/eur-lex/lex/LexUriServ/site/en/com/2002/com2002_0667en01.pdf</ext-link>. Accessed 18 Apr 2006</comment></element-citation></ref><ref id="pone.0002519-Kondilis1"><label>16</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kondilis</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Soteriades</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Falagas</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><year>2006</year><article-title>Health Literacy Research in Europe: A Brief Snapshot.</article-title><source>Eur J Public Health</source><volume>16</volume><fpage>113</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16230315</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="pone.0002519-Soteriades1"><label>17</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Soteriades</surname><given-names>ES</given-names></name><name><surname>Falagas</surname><given-names>ME</given-names></name></person-group><year>2005</year><article-title>Comparison of amount of biomedical research originating from the European Union and the United States.</article-title><source>Brit Med J</source><volume>331</volume><fpage>192</fpage><lpage>4</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16037452</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="pone.0002519-Vergidis1"><label>18</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Vergidis</surname><given-names>PI</given-names></name><name><surname>Karavasiou</surname><given-names>AI</given-names></name><name><surname>Paraschakis</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Bliziotis</surname><given-names>IA</given-names></name><name><surname>Falagas</surname><given-names>ME</given-names></name></person-group><year>2005</year><article-title>Bibliometric analysis of global trends for research productivity in microbiology.</article-title><source>Eur J Clin Microbiol Infect Dis</source><volume>24</volume><fpage>342</fpage><lpage>6</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15834594</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="pone.0002519-Falagas1"><label>19</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Falagas</surname><given-names>ME</given-names></name><name><surname>Papastamataki</surname><given-names>PA</given-names></name><name><surname>Bliziotis</surname><given-names>IA</given-names></name></person-group><year>2006</year><article-title>A bibliometric analysis of research productivity in Parasitology by different world regions during a 9-year period (1995&#x02013;2003).</article-title><source>BMC Infect Dis</source><volume>6</volume><fpage>56</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16545114</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="pone.0002519-Mastilica1"><label>20</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Mastilica</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Kusec</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><year>2005</year><article-title>Croatian healthcare system in transition, from the perspective of users.</article-title><source>Brit Med J</source><volume>331</volume><fpage>223</fpage><lpage>6</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16037464</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="pone.0002519-Author1"><label>21</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><collab>[Author unlisted]</collab><year>2005</year><article-title>Taking health literacy seriously.</article-title><volume>366</volume><fpage>95</fpage></element-citation></ref><ref id="pone.0002519-European2"><label>22</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><collab>European Commission</collab><year>2001</year><article-title>The eLearning Action Plan. Designing tomorrow's education. Communication from the Commission to the council and the European Parliament. 28 March 2001, Brussels.</article-title><comment>Available: <ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://europa.eu.int/eur-lex/en/com/cnc/2001/com2001_0172en01.pdf">http://europa.eu.int/eur-lex/en/com/cnc/2001/com2001_0172en01.pdf</ext-link>. Accessed 18 Apr 2006</comment></element-citation></ref><ref id="pone.0002519-European3"><label>23</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><collab>European Commission</collab><year>2002b</year><article-title>eEurope 2005:An information society for all. An Action Plan to be presented in view of the Sevilla European Council21/22 June 2002. Communication from the Commission to the Council, the European Parliament, the Economic and Social Committee and the Committee of Regions. 28 May 2002, Brussels.</article-title><comment>Available: <ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://europa.eu.int/information_society/eeurope/2002/news_library/documents/eeurope2005/eeurope2005_en.pdf">http://europa.eu.int/information_society/eeurope/2002/news_library/documents/eeurope2005/eeurope2005_en.pdf</ext-link>. Accessed 18 Apr 2006</comment></element-citation></ref><ref id="pone.0002519-Kickbusch1"><label>24</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kickbusch</surname><given-names>IS</given-names></name></person-group><year>2001</year><article-title>Health literacy: Addressing the health and education divide.</article-title><source>Health Promotion International</source><volume>16</volume><fpage>289</fpage><lpage>97</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11509466</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="pone.0002519-Kusec1"><label>25</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kusec</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Brborovic</surname><given-names>O</given-names></name><name><surname>Schillinger</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name></person-group><year>2003</year><article-title>Diabetes websites accredited by the Health on the Net Foundation Code of Conduct: Readable or not?</article-title><source>Stud Health Technol Inform</source><volume>95</volume><fpage>655</fpage><lpage>60</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14664062</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="pone.0002519-European4"><label>26</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><comment>European Health Forum Gastein website. Available: <ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.ehfg.org/typo3/index.php?id=56&#x00026;L=2">www.ehfg.org/typo3/index.php?id=56&#x00026;L=2</ext-link>. Accessed 2 Apr 2006</comment></element-citation></ref><ref id="pone.0002519-Mierzewski1"><label>27</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Mierzewski</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name></person-group><year>2005</year><article-title>Patients' empowerment: The East side Story.</article-title><source>Brit Med J</source><volume>331</volume><fpage>226</fpage><lpage>7</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16037465</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="pone.0002519-Mika1"><label>28</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Mika</surname><given-names>VS</given-names></name><name><surname>Kelly</surname><given-names>PJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Price</surname><given-names>MA</given-names></name><name><surname>Franquiz</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Villarreal</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><year>2005</year><article-title>The ABCs of health literacy.</article-title><source>Fam Community Health</source><volume>28</volume><fpage>351</fpage><lpage>7</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16166862</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="pone.0002519-Young1"><label>29</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Young</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name></person-group><year>2004</year><article-title>Low health literacy is high among Americans, studies say.</article-title><source>Am J Health Syst Pharm</source><volume>61</volume><fpage>986</fpage><lpage>7</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15160772</pub-id></element-citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>